                                                "sense_id": "8e8397d0-50c1-36cd-b36c-ee213de092eb",
                                                "text": "The Britannia Tubular Bridge is immediately west of Menai Bridge Station on the Holyhead main line. In design it consists of two continuous box girders of rectangular cross section, one for each track. It was opened in 1850."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f62c1cf-e83c-4d2d-8c1f-e2f13064fd34",
                                                "sense_id": "8e8397d0-50c1-36cd-b36c-ee213de092eb",
                                                "text": "An all-welded, box section underframe, incorporating box girders which run the full length of the locomotive, is welded to stress-bearing bodysides with partition walls forming reinforcing cross members."
